 and \begin_inset Formula $z_t=\rho_z z_{t-1}+\omega_t$\end_inset
, where \begin_inset Formula $|\rho_u|,|\rho_\eta|,|\rho_z|<1$\end_inset
. Each process is initialized in its stationary law. The three innovation sequences are mutually independent across processes and dates, centered, bounded and have finite variance. The three stationary processes are independent of one another; their supports and intercepts ensure positive clearing prices and quantities. You may use the stationary moment law of large numbers for these processes. Does contemporaneous \begin_inset Formula $z_t$\end_inset
 remain a valid demand instrument? Derive \begin_inset Formula $\operatorname{Cov}(p_{t-1},u_t)$\end_inset
 and assess whether lagged price is automatically a valid and relevant instrument. Explain why correcting standard errors for serial correlation cannot repair an invalid instrument. Does the simultaneity problem here require stochastic trends or dynamic optimization? [12]
