. Delivered prices are \begin_inset Formula $p_{ij}=p_it_{ij}$\end_inset
. There are no outside transfers or trade deficits. Destination \begin_inset Formula $j$\end_inset
 chooses nonnegative delivered quantities \begin_inset Formula $c_{ij}$\end_inset
 with budget \begin_inset Formula $\sum_i p_it_{ij}c_{ij}\leq y_j$\end_inset
 and utility \begin_inset Formula $U_j(c)=[\sum_i\beta_i^{(1-\sigma)/\sigma}c_{ij}^{(\sigma-1)/\sigma}]^{\sigma/(\sigma-1)}$\end_inset
, where \begin_inset Formula $\beta_i>0$\end_inset
 and \begin_inset Formula $\sigma>0$\end_inset
, \begin_inset Formula $\sigma\ne1$\end_inset
. For \begin_inset Formula $0<\sigma<1$\end_inset
, define utility to be zero when any component is zero, its continuous boundary value. You may use the standard concavity of this CES aggregator. Bilateral expenditure is \begin_inset Formula $x_{ij}=p_it_{ij}c_{ij}$\end_inset
, including domestic expenditure when \begin_inset Formula $i=j$\end_inset
. Let \begin_inset Formula $Y=\sum_i y_i$\end_inset
 and \begin_inset Formula $\theta_i=y_i/Y$\end_inset
.
