\begin_layout Exercise*
There is one consumption good, whose price is one, fixed land \begin_inset Formula $X>0$\end_inset
, and a mass \begin_inset Formula $N>0$\end_inset
 of identical current adults with skill \begin_inset Formula $h>0$\end_inset
. A competitive constant returns firm rents land \begin_inset Formula $Z\geq0$\end_inset
 and raw adult labor hours \begin_inset Formula $L\geq0$\end_inset
 to produce \begin_inset Formula $Y=A Z^{1-\alpha}(hL)^\alpha$\end_inset
, where \begin_inset Formula $A>0$\end_inset
 and \begin_inset Formula $0<\alpha<1$\end_inset
. The land market must clear at \begin_inset Formula $Z=X$\end_inset
. The wage \begin_inset Formula $w>0$\end_inset
 is paid per raw hour, and \begin_inset Formula $R$\end_inset
 is rent per unit of land. Every adult owns an equal land share and receives \begin_inset Formula $\rho=RX/N$\end_inset
. Firm profit is distributed but is zero at a competitive supporting price.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Exercise*
Each adult has one unit of time. It chooses consumption \begin_inset Formula $c>0$\end_inset
, continuous fertility \begin_inset Formula $n>0$\end_inset
 and education time per child \begin_inset Formula $e\geq0$\end_inset
 to maximize \begin_inset Formula $(1-\gamma)\log c+\gamma\log[n h_a(e)]$\end_inset
, where \begin_inset Formula $0<\gamma<1$\end_inset
, \begin_inset Formula $\tau>0$\end_inset
, \begin_inset Formula $a>0$\end_inset
, \begin_inset Formula $\overline c>0$\end_inset
 and \begin_inset Formula $h_a(e)=1+ae/(\tau+e)$\end_inset
. Total child time is \begin_inset Formula $t=n(\tau+e)$\end_inset
. Constraints are \begin_inset Formula $c+wt\leq w+\rho$\end_inset
, \begin_inset Formula $t\leq1$\end_inset
 and \begin_inset Formula $c\geq\overline c$\end_inset
. Land rent is nonlabor income: child time sacrifices wages, not rent. Each household takes \begin_inset Formula $w$\end_inset
 and \begin_inset Formula $\rho$\end_inset
 as given. The logarithm excludes zero fertility in this model.
\end_layout

